"பண்ணற்","parts":[{"text":"பண்ணற்","lemma":"பண்ணற்","gloss":"about Paṇṇaṉ"}],"gloss":"about Paṇṇaṉ","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கேட்டிரோ","parts":[{"text":"கேட்டிரோ","lemma":"கேட்டிரோ","gloss":"did you hear?"}],"gloss":"did you hear?","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"avaṉ","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"his"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வினைப்பகடு","parts":[{"text":"வினை","lemma":"viṉai","gloss":"work"},{"text":"பகடு","lemma":"pakaṭu","gloss":"bull"}],"gloss":"working bull"},{"surface":"ஏற்ற","parts":[{"text":"ஏற்ற","lemma":"ஏற்ற","gloss":"suitable"}],"gloss":"suitable","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மேழிக்","parts":[{"text":"மேழிக்","lemma":"மேழிக்","gloss":"of the plow-tail"}],"gloss":"of the plow-tail","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிணைத்தொடா","parts":[{"text":"கிணை","lemma":"kiṇai","gloss":"drum"},{"text":"தொடு","lemma":"toṭu","gloss":"bind"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"adjective suffix"}],"gloss":"drum-strap"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நாடொறும்","parts":[{"text":"நாடொறும்","lemma":"நாடொறும்","gloss":"every day"}],"gloss":"every day","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பாடேன்","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"ஏன்","lemma":"ēṉ","gloss":"first person singular negative"}],"gloss":"I will not sing"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if"},{"surface":"ஆனா","parts":[{"text":"ஆனா","lemma":"āṉā","gloss":"unceasing"}],"gloss":"unceasing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணிகிளர்","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"maṇi","gloss":"gem"},{"text":"கிளர்","lemma":"kiḷar","gloss":"shine"}],"gloss":"shining with gems"},{"surface":"முன்றில்","parts":[{"text":"முன்றில்","lemma":"முன்றில்","gloss":"courtyard"}],"gloss":"courtyard","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தென்னவன்","parts":[{"text":"தென்னவன்","lemma":"தென்னவன்","gloss":"the Southern King"}],"gloss":"the Southern King","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மருகன்","parts":[{"text":"மருகன்","lemma":"marukaṉ","gloss":"descendant"}],"gloss":"descendant"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிணிமுரசு","parts":[{"text":"பிணி","lemma":"piṇi","gloss":"bind"},{"text":"முரசு","lemma":"murasu","gloss":"drum"}],"gloss":"bound war-drum"},{"surface":"இரங்கும்","parts":[{"text":"இரங்கு","lemma":"irangku","gloss":"sound"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"habitual adjective suffix"}],"gloss":"sounding"},{"surface":"பீடுகெழு","parts":[{"text":"பீடு","lemma":"pīṭu","gloss":"greatness"},{"text":"கெழு","lemma":"keḻu","gloss":"possess"}],"gloss":"greatness-possessing"},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"tāṉai","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"army"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"aṇṇal","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"வழுதி","parts":[{"text":"வழுதி","lemma":"vaḻuti","gloss":"Vaḻuti"}],"gloss":"Vaḻuti"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கண்மாறிலியர்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"māṟu","gloss":"change"},{"text":"இலி","lemma":"ili","gloss":"without"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"ar","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may he not turn his eyes away"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"பெருங்கிளைப்","parts":[{"text":"பெருங்கிளைப்","lemma":"பெருங்கிளைப்","gloss":"large family"}],"gloss":"large family","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புரவே","parts":[{"text":"புரவு","lemma":"puravu","gloss":"protection"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"protection"}]}],"literal":"Venus in the southern region staying, fertile fields / low-lying lands withered, at the useless time, / the drummer with the large drum who went, his great name / Paṇṇaṉ, the lord of the small village, approaching, / as one who knows his own state, in that state / distress fleeing to go, possessing / he who gave, my father, the noble lord of excellence in giving, / like the tongue-tusk of an elephant with a fine rope and large trunk, / the winning truthful words, the fertile land with grass / plowing Paṇṇaṉ, did you hear of him? / The working bull yoked to the plow-tail, with the drum-strap, / every day if I do not sing, unceasing / in the courtyard shining with gems, the descendant of the Southern King, / with the army of great pride where the bound war-drum roars, / Vaḻuti of majestic elephants, / may he not turn his eyes away from protecting my large family.","translation":"When Venus moves to the south and fertile fields in low-lying lands wither in a season of drought, the drummer with his large drum goes to Paṇṇaṉ, the lord of the small village. Understanding his plight, Paṇṇaṉ gives generously so that his distress flees. He is my father, a noble lord of giving. Like the powerful trunk of an elephant guided by a fine rope, his truthful words conquer, turning even barren lands into fertile fields. Have you heard of him? If I do not sing of Paṇṇaṉ every day, yoking my drum-strap like a working bull to a plow, then may Vaḻuti—the Pandya king of majestic elephants, whose army has roaring war-drums and whose gem-strewn courtyard shines—turn his eyes away and cease to protect my large family!","modern":"வெள்ளி கோள் தெற்கு திசையில் தங்கி, விளைநிலங்களும் பள்ளங்களும் காய்ந்து வறண்ட பயனில்லாத பஞ்ச காலத்தில், பெரிய பறையை உடைய கிணைமகன் சிறுகுடிக்குத் தலைவனான பண்ணனைச் சென்றடைந்தான். தன் நிலையை உணர்ந்து, வறுமை ஓடிப் போகுமாறு வாரி வழங்கிய வள்ளல் என் தந்தையாகிய பண்ணன் ஆவான். பாகனின் நுண்ணிய கயிற்றால் கட்டுப்படும் யானையின் தும்பிக்கையைப் போல, அவனது வாய்மை மொழியால் புல்லுடைய விளைநிலங்களை உழுது பண்படுத்தும் பண்ணனைப் பற்றி கேள்விப்பட்டிருக்கிறீர்களா? உழவு மாடு ஏர்க்காலில் பூட்டப்படுவது போல, என் கிணைக் கருவியைக் கட்டிக்கொண்டு நாள்தோறும் அவனைப் பாடாவிட்டால், மணிகள் பதித்த முற்றத்தைக் கொண்டவனும், போர் முரசுகள் முழங்கும் படையை உடையவனுமான பாண்டிய மன்னன் வழுதி என் பெரிய சுற்றத்தைக் காப்பதைத் தவிர்த்து, தன் பார்வையைத் திருப்பிக் கொள்ளட்டும்.","explanation":"This poem is in the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai and Iyaṉmoḻi tuṟai, where the poet Madurai Aḷakkar Ñāḻār Makaṉār Maḷḷaṉār praises the extraordinary generosity of Ciṟukuṭikiḻāṉ Paṇṇaṉ. The poet describes a severe drought when Venus moves south, causing low-lying fields to wither. In this desperate time, a drummer approaches Paṇṇaṉ, who immediately relieves his distress with boundless gifts. The poet declares that if he does not sing of Paṇṇaṉ's glory every single day, he deserves to lose the patronage of the great Pandya king, Vaḻuti. This dramatic oath highlights the poet's deep gratitude and the supreme status of Paṇṇaṉ's benevolence, which surpasses even royal patronage.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}